75:| [`spec-reviewer`](agents/spec-reviewer.md) | sonnet | Read, Glob, Grep, Bash, Write | Reviews a plan or implementation against the project's canonical requirement specs (openspec/specs/ or docs/specs/) and returns one verdict with a per-requirement coverage table, flagging scope creep (work no requirement asks for) and gaps (required scenarios not delivered). Use when a change implements or extends an existing capability, someone asks "spec review" or "check against the requirements", or before approving a plan/diff that cites a spec. |
77:| [`test-coverage-reviewer`](agents/test-coverage-reviewer.md) | sonnet | Read, Glob, Grep, Bash, Write | Analyzes a diff's test coverage behaviorally, not by line %: maps each new or changed behavior to a test that would go red, scores gaps 1-10 and flags tests that only test the mock. Returns one verdict. Use when someone asks "are tests missing?", "is coverage enough?", "what regression would slip through?", or before approving a diff touching business logic, validation, auth or a cross-process flow. |
78:| [`test-runner`](agents/test-runner.md) | sonnet | Read, Glob, Grep, Bash, Write | Runs the project's whole unit suite and its coverage command, apart from the implementer, and records each command, its exit code, its summary and the coverage against the target in the change's unit-tests.md. Edits no file but that one. Use when a change's unit-tests stage is next, after the implementation — "run the unit tests of this change", "check the coverage against the target". |
86:| [`e2e-testing`](skills/e2e-testing/SKILL.md) | Writes end-to-end tests from a change's acceptance criteria and specs, without reading the tests its diff adds, runs the project's declared E2E command and records each scenario against its criterion. Use when a change's code is done and its E2E command is declared, or when someone asks for end-to-end coverage of the acceptance criteria — "write E2E tests for this change", "exercise the criteria end to end". |
93:| [`test-and-coverage`](skills/test-and-coverage/SKILL.md) | Discovers the repo's test surfaces and their commands, runs them per surface with coverage, reports PASS/WARN/FAIL against the coverage target, and analyzes gaps with prioritized test suggestions. Use when validating an implementation, before a commit or PR, or when the user says "run the tests", "test this surface", "check coverage", "coverage report", "what's untested", "which files need tests". |
